// Per-developer signing. tools/config-local.sh copies this file to
// Config/Local.xcconfig (gitignored) on the first build, and Config/Base.xcconfig
// includes that copy if it exists. Edit the copy, never this template.
//
// The defaults below are ad-hoc signing, the same thing CI passes on the command line.
// They build and run every target on the machine that produced them, so a fresh
// checkout works without any setup.
//
// Ad-hoc signing gives the binary a new code signature on every build, so macOS treats
// each build as a new application and re-asks for the permissions the UI tests and the
// screenshot tooling need. Signing with a real Apple Development identity keeps those
// grants across builds. To do that, set both values below: the identity exactly as
// `security find-identity -v -p codesigning` prints it, and your ten-character Team ID
// from https://developer.apple.com/account (Membership details).
//
//   OPENSKY_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
//   OPENSKY_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345

OPENSKY_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
OPENSKY_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
